contentText:
Justin Timberlake and Jessica Biel are in it for the long haul. The A-list couple each posted loving tribute to each other on Sunday (Oct. 4) to commemorate their 14th wedding anniversary. In separate Instagram Story posts, the stars shared a rare glimpse into their private life, including a cute skiing photo with their sons, Silas, 11 and Phineas, 6.

Timberlake&#8217;s post opened with a cute pic of the couple holding hands as they walk along a city street cued to James Taylor&#8217;s &#8220;How Sweet It Is (To Be Loved By You)&#8221; with the message &#8220;Happy Anniversary ❤️ @Jessicabiel.&#8221; The next photo included a bug-eyed Biel, 44 looking out from behind a black red light therapy mask with the caption &#8220;My favorite person in every lifetime,&#8221; this time cued to Carl Carlton&#8217;s Grammy-nominated 1982 funk soul classic &#8220;She&#8217;s a Bad Mama Jama (She&#8217;s Built, She&#8217;s Stacked).&#8221;

The rest of the reel runs through a shot of Biel snuggling with Phineas as Timberlake, 45, puts a gentle hand on the back of Silas&#8217; head — with the caption &#8220;and the greatest mom&#8221; — and concludes with a smiling picture of Biel hugging Timberlake from behind captioned &#8220;14 Down. Forever to go.&#8221;

Biel was having all the feels as well, reposting the hand in hand pic from Timberlake&#8217;s feed, as well as a throwback snap of the couple in which she&#8217;s throwing up a peace sign with the dedication, &#8220;Happy anniversary my love @justintimberlake ❤️.&#8221; She also gave the &#8220;SexyBack&#8221; singer some parental props, including a pic of the singer on the ski slopes with the boys captioned &#8220;The best dad 🥇.&#8221;

Her post ended on a super sweet note, with a simple &#8220;I love you ❤️&#8221; message and a snap of her planting a kiss on a smiling Timberlake&#8217;s face. Biel and Timberlake started dating in 2007 and briefly split in March 2011 before reuniting later that year, and getting engaged in Dec. 2011. They married in southern Italy in October 2012.

Timberlake has mostly been laying low since ending his Forget Tomorrow World tour last summer in support of his Everything I Thought It Was studio album, revealing after its conclusion that he was suffering from the effects of Lyme disease . Her popped back out unexpectedly in January to perform at the Recording Academy Honors Black Music Collective event honoring old friend and frequent collaborator Pharrell Williams, and then again in August when he made a surprise cameo at Don Toliver&#8217;s show in Miami and once more last month when he performed &#8220;Until the End of Time&#8221; and &#8220;Holy Grail&#8221; at Jay-Z&#8217;s Paris gig celebrating the 30th anniversary of the rapper&#8217;s Reasonable Doubt album.

The singer also appears on Migos member and solo star Quavo’s just-released QRÖMELIFE album on the bubbling R&B jam &#8220;House Music.&#8221;
